<section>
    <h2 class="Toolkit-sectionTitle">Getting started</h2>

    <div class="Toolkit-prose">
        <div class="Story-warning">
            <strong>Read this page, then delete it.</strong> It belongs to the starter kit, not to
            your project — hence its <em>waiting</em> status. Deleting
            <code>components/Toolkit/getting-started.html.twig</code> retires the page, navigation
            entry included; its lines in <code>ComponentStatus</code> and
            <code>ToolkitController::SECTIONS</code> stay behind harmlessly until you drop them.
        </div>

        <p>
            The toolkit renders one page per component, from the stories it finds on disk. It
            answers only while the kernel runs in debug: a live shop returns a 404.
        </p>

        <h3>Adding a story</h3>

        <p>
            Drop a <code>toolkit.html.twig</code> next to the component it shows, say in
            <code>components/Molecules/Button/</code>. Nothing to register — the folder path becomes
            the page name and its URL.
        </p>

        <h3>Saying where a story stands</h3>

        <p>
            Statuses live in <code>src/Toolkit/ComponentStatus.php</code>, keyed by the story path
            under <code>components/</code>. The list ships empty, and a story absent from it claims
            nothing. <strong>It is not a backlog</strong> — only a way to say what has been settled.
        </p>

        <ul class="Toolkit-legend">
            <li class="Toolkit-legendRow">
                <span class="Toolkit-statusBadge Toolkit-statusBadge--ready">ready</span>
                <span>Handled on our side and open to review — not reviewed yet.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="Toolkit-legendRow">
                <span class="Toolkit-statusBadge Toolkit-statusBadge--waiting">waiting</span>
                <span>
                    Stopped on something that is not the theme's to decide. A status cannot say
                    <em>what</em>, so the story carries a banner that does — the one above.
                </span>
            </li>
            <li class="Toolkit-legendRow">
                <span class="Toolkit-statusBadge">hidden</span>
                <span>
                    Never to be integrated: the story is dropped from the toolkit. The files stay,
                    CSS import included — removing it while a call site remains would leave the
                    component unstyled.
                </span>
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Previewing at a width</h3>

        <p>
            The selector above the navigation renders the current page in an iframe at a chosen
            breakpoint, and keeps that width as you move between components.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
